{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792882277,"nonce":"mjnaqnR7CCj9JDBVk4bykcqp6zo=","message":"Implemented missing CSS paint-state and lifecycle ownership handling, grouped with promoted-source final-property delivery.\n\nRenderContext records active animation/transition membership and promotion ownership per layout node across public frames. Changes invalidate existing cached geometry and static pixels before replay. Visible nontransparent active output with neither a CSS paint record nor a baked texture also requests a full walk. Unchanged transparent/offscreen output does not trigger this missing-state invalidation. Two maps reuse their allocations between snapshots; inner compositor paint calls do not take another lifecycle snapshot. Existing cache invalidation and stale promoted-texture release perform the handoff. Promotion policy and shader/data layouts are unchanged.\n\nLayout property application now remembers sampled promoted sources as well as non-promoted sources, so their final values are delivered once after completion. The composite-eligibility predicate waits for stopped sampled sources to write final properties, while playing baked sources remain eligible. Completed entries do not overwrite later ordinary property writes.\n\nNegative evidence before production edits:\n- All four new public lifecycle tests failed. Initially transparent compositor output stayed [0,0,255,255] at a later 0.5 opacity, expected [0,128,128,255]. A source started over an existing cache stayed opaque [0,255,0,255] instead of half opacity. Completion replay froze at [0,128,128,255] instead of [0,191,64,255]. A promoted source stopped with render opacity 0.75 instead of final 0.6. Log: /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-negative-app.log.\n- The new layout completion test failed because css_has_active became false before a promoted source's final values were applied. Log: /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-negative-layout.log.\n\nFinal scoped validation:\n- Five lifecycle app tests pass normally and with both GPU storage flags forced off (data textures). Keyframes and transitions cover direct/compositor public frames, transparent first paint with/without another CSS record, delayed source start over cached static content, final-value completion, observed restart, removal with base property restoration, promotion -\u003e native -\u003e promotion -\u003e completion, and stale bake release. Every displayed state also has an unchanged-frame replay. Property application uses the normal RenderTree CSS apply methods, with deterministic current values rather than wall-clock scheduler ticks.\n- Cache-preservation control checks the ownership gate keeps unchanged transparent/offscreen cached geometry, and settled frames retain their cache after completion. Viewport is explicit. The missing-state check does not force repaint solely because an unchanged offscreen or transparent node lacks metadata.\n- All six tests in the touched blinc_layout css_layer_bake integration file pass, including the new animation/transition promoted completion control. It checks playing baked eligibility, pending final delivery, exact final opacity and that later ordinary property writes are not overwritten by a completed source.\n- Adjacent normal app controls pass: opacity_groups_css (4), composite_layers (8), retained foreground CSS repaint (1), static group suppression of CSS child promotion (1). With five new app cases, that is 19 app tests plus six layout tests normally; five app cases also pass in DT.\n- CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, fallback capacities 1024, offscreen only. Touched-file rustfmt and diff checks pass. New production module css_cache_lifecycle.rs is 61 lines; context shell is 821 lines, and touched extracted production modules stay below 1000. Temporary GPU capability overrides restored; no GPU source diff. App/layout CHANGELOG entries updated. No workspace/DSL/docs/platform or unrelated gates.\n\nLogs: /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-normal-app.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-normal-layout.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-normal-opacity_groups_css.log, /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-normal-composite_layers.log, two adjacent normal guard logs, and /private/tmp/blinc-css-lifecycle-dt-css_lifecycle.log. Driver: /private/tmp/blinc_css_lifecycle_modes.py.\n\nCost/limits: two reusable ownership maps hold node ids and three booleans per active CSS owner, retaining peak allocated capacity. Snapshot comparison scans active owners. Source/promotion changes require a full paint; steady ownership keeps existing patch/bake reuse. Layout sampled-source sets now also include promoted active sources. No timing or byte-allocation benchmark, browser/mobile or scheduler interpolation claim. The direct active-CSS path retains its prior conservative full walk. This models ownership changes observed between frames; same-frame replacement with unchanged membership/promotion identity is not a new animation-generation mechanism. Tree/window id isolation remains separate.\n\nRemaining parent scope: cross-stream group isolation, collected text/SVG/ImageElement, separate GPU passes/3D meshes, named Sample and other mixed-cache/animation ownership. No push.","files":null}]}